    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d334">

                <pb facs="0554" n="452" xml:id="pg452"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">500.C1197/907: Telegram (part air)</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Consul at Geneva</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Gilbert</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Geneva</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1935-10-29T16:00:00+01:00">October 29, 1935—4
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received October 30—12:50 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>551. Consulate’s 498, October 14, 6 p.m.<anchor n="16" xml:id="d334-f1"/>
                </p>
                <list>
                    <label>1.</label>
                    <item>Ekstrand<anchor n="17" xml:id="d334-f2"/> has now communicated to all
                        members of the Advisory Committee a note in the form of document O C 1612 A
                        covering the following points: <list>
                            <label>(<hi rendition="#italic">a</hi>)</label>
                            <item>In view of the replies received as indicated in my telegram under
                                reference the chairman of the Advisory Committee has decided to
                                cancel the autumn session.</item>
                            <label>(<hi rendition="#italic">b</hi>)</label>
                            <item>The majority of the members have raised no objection to the date
                                of March 14 for the next session. Nevertheless, others have called
                                attention to inconveniences and disadvantages of that date. In view
                                of the latter considerations Ekstrand in agreement with the Chairman
                                now suggests that the 21st session should begin on May 15 and the
                                seizures subcommittee on May 7.</item>
                            <label>(<hi rendition="#italic">c</hi>)</label>
                            <item>The members of the Committee are requested to inform the Director
                                of the Opium Section before December 15 whether they agree to these
                                dates.</item>
                        </list>
                    </item>
                    <label>2.</label>
                    <item>Copies of this document mailed to Fuller today.<anchor n="18"
                            xml:id="d334-f3"/>
                    </item>
                </list>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Gilbert</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d334-f1" n="16" xml:id="d334-f1-content">
                <p>Not printed.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d334-f2" n="17" xml:id="d334-f2-content">
                <p>Eric Einar Ekstrand, Director of the Opium Traffic and Social Traffic Sections of
                    the League of Nations.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d334-f3" n="18" xml:id="d334-f3-content">
                <p>The Consul at Geneva reported in his telegram No. 55, February 7, 1936, 3 p.m.:
                    “Ekstrand has now sent out the circular letter informing governments that the
                    21st session of the Opium Advisory Committee will open on May 18 and the
                    subcommittee on seizures on May 11.” (500.C1197/932)</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
